@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
title PLAN — multi-provider broker: one route table, no pinned provider

node "TODAY — one pin, N-1 sentinels" as NOW <<error>> {
  component "broker.Config\nHosts · Header · Value\nONE provider" as OLD <<app>>
  component "modelPinnedProvider\nheuristic chooses the pin" as PIN <<app>>
  component "ambiguousBareIDs\nrefuses to guess" as AMB <<app>>
  component "container holds\nproveo-brokered for\nEVERY other key" as SENT <<error>>
}

node "PLANNED — a route per provider" as NEW <<host>> {
  component "broker.Config\nRoutes []Route · Strip" as CFG <<app>>
  component "Route\nHosts · Header · Query · Value" as RT <<app>>
  component "Apply(req)\nmatch host -> inject that route\nno match -> strip" as APPLY <<app>>
}

database "inject/broker.env\nalready holds EVERY key\n0600, outside every agent mount" as ENV <<db>>

OLD ARROW_MAIN PIN : needs exactly one
PIN ARROW_OPTIONAL AMB
OLD ARROW_ERROR SENT : the bug the operator sees
CFG ARROW_MAIN RT : one per detected provider
RT ARROW_MAIN APPLY
ENV ARROW_MAIN CFG : the file is already right

note bottom of SENT
  **The failure this removes.** ""ARCHITECT_MODEL=kimi-3"" with
  ""EDITOR_MODEL=grok-4.5"" needs moonshot AND xai in one session.
  Whichever gets pinned wins; the other receives the literal
  ""proveo-brokered"" and the harness reports an invalid API key.
  Nothing in the topology is wrong — the config shape simply
  cannot express two providers.
end note

note bottom of CFG
  **This landed.** ""brokerProviders"" returns the whole detected set and
  ""broker\.Config"" carries ""Routes"" — one entry per broker-injectable
  provider, in registry order — so the right-hand node is the shipped
  shape and the left-hand one is history. What follows is the history
  worth keeping, recovered from the ""main\.go"" prose it replaced.

  **The old shape and its failure.** It used to pin exactly one
  provider, falling back to a model-name heuristic when several keys
  were present. That made a //correct// multi-provider "".env"" fail:
  the unpinned providers received the sentinel and the harness reported
  an invalid API key. Returning the whole set is what lets a session
  whose roles span vendors authenticate — each key is injected only
  toward its own provider's hosts, so N routes carry the same guarantee
  as one did.

  **The warning shrank with it.** The "several providers, broker pins
  one" warning is gone; several providers is the supported shape, not a
  caveat. What ""brokerOffReason"" still explains is the one posture
  where the container holds sentinels with //nothing// brokering them —
  keys detected but none broker-injectable, or the broker disabled
  through ""PROVEO_CREDENTIAL_BROKER"" — because from inside the
  container that is indistinguishable from a bad key, and the way out
  is ""--credentials forward"".
end note

note right of APPLY
  **The invariant that makes this safe.** A key is injected only on a
  request whose destination matches ITS OWN route. Provider A's secret
  can never appear on a request to provider B — the same property the
  single-pin broker had, applied N times rather than once.

  Off-route requests still strip ""DefaultStripHeaders"". Unchanged.

  Route matching stays suffix-based on the verified host, so the
  existing ""isProviderHost"" logic is reused per route rather than
  reimplemented.
end note

note as Blast #F4F9FB
  **The honest tradeoff.** Blast radius widens from one provider's budget
  to N. It is a smaller step than it looks:

  * **Reach was already N.** The Squid allowlist covers every detected
    provider, because a session may switch model mid-run. Only the
    //credential// was pinned.
  * **""forward"" is strictly worse** and is the current workaround — it puts
    all N real keys inside the container.

  So this lands between the two, and is the first posture that both serves
  a multi-provider session AND keeps every key out of the container.

  **Narrowing stays available**: ""--providers moonshot,xai"" restricts the
  route table explicitly. Opt-in, not a heuristic.
end note

note bottom of AMB
  **What this deletes.** ""modelPinnedProvider"" and ""ambiguousBareIDs"" exist
  ONLY because injection needed a single winner. With a route per provider
  there is nothing to disambiguate: a model id that cannot be attributed
  no longer breaks a run.

  Their remaining use is advisory — see the model catalog plan — where a
  wrong guess costs a warning instead of a 401. Heuristics belong on the
  warning path, never on the credential path. This codebase has now been
  bitten twice by one on the credential path.

  **As shipped: ""modelPinnedProvider"" is now deleted.** The credential
  path had already stopped calling it — ""brokerProviders"" returns the
  whole detected set — so it sat in ""cmd/proveo/main\.go"" as a definition
  with no caller until the prose migration noticed. Removing it was
  bookkeeping, not a behavior change.

  Its reasoning is not lost: a model id //names// its provider, so a host
  holding five keys but pointed at ""claude-opus-5"" is unambiguously an
  anthropic run, and roles that disagree refuse the pin rather than
  guess. That is recorded in the ""BrokerPin"" note of
  ""_spec/internal/egress/egress-tiers\.puml"", which is where the rule
  belongs now that no single function owns it.
end note

note bottom of ENV
  **No new secret handling.** ""writeBrokerEnv"" already writes every detected
  key to this file; only the reader's config shape changes. The DLP scanner
  improves for free: it can require each secret to appear only toward its
  own provider's hosts, instead of scanning against a single pin.
end note
@enduml
